# Main Content Bottom Corners (Inset Layout)

When building or updating pages/components that render in the main content area (inside `SidebarInset` in the `(main)` layout), keep the **bottom corners** visually consistent:

- **Desktop (md and up)**: main content containers should have **rounded bottom corners**, matching the homepage look.
- **Mobile**: bottom corners may be square (no rounding) unless the design explicitly calls for it.

## Implementation Guidelines

- Prefer applying the rounding on the **top-level container for the page content**, not on nested cards, so the whole content area clips correctly.
- Use responsive Tailwind classes like:
  - `rounded-b-none md:rounded-b-xl` on the outermost content wrapper.
  - Pair with `overflow-hidden` when content (e.g. iframes, full-bleed sections) needs to respect the rounded corners.
- Align the background color and rounding with existing pages (e.g. home) so the shell feels consistent when adding new pages like detail views, long-form content, or embedded experiences.

